Package: blockr.script
Title: Script and Prose Blocks for 'blockr'
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    c(person(given = "Christoph",
             family = "Sax",
             role = c("aut", "cre"),
             email = "christoph@cynkra.com"),
      person(given = "Nicolas",
             family = "Bennett",
             role = "aut",
             email = "nicolas@cynkra.com"),
      person(given = "Bristol Myers Squibb", role = c("fnd", "cph")))
Description: A block for 'blockr' boards whose state is an ordinary R
    script. The script reads any number of upstream results and returns
    whatever its last statement evaluates to. A top-level assignment of a
    plain value becomes a control on the block, and the exported code is the
    script with the current values written in. A prose block holds
    markdown with inline R, as 'Quarto' writes it, and reads its inputs the
    same way.
